node_modules
dist
# NOTE: `client/` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is build output, which would
# normally never be committed — but Catalyst hosts this repo's `main` branch
# directly, so the folder it serves has to exist in the branch. Regenerate it
# with `npm run build:catalyst` and commit the result whenever the app changes,
# or the deployed site silently lags the source.
#
# If Catalyst is ever reconfigured to run the build itself, ignore `client`
# again and delete it from the tree — committed build output is a cost, not a
# convention.
canon-static
storybook-static
*.local
.DS_Store
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
canon.log
*.log
